---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Best SIM Card & eSIM for Tourists in China";
const description = "Compare eSIM and physical SIM options for China — Airalo, Holafly, China Mobile, and more.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="th">
 <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
 <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
 <a href="/th/life/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
 <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
 <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
 </svg>
 Back to ชีวิต
 </a>
 </nav>
 <header class="mb-12">
 <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">📶 ชีวิตในจีน</p>
 <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
 Best SIM Card & eSIM<br class="hidden md:block" /> for Tourists in China
 </h1>
 <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">eSIM, physical SIM, or roaming — which one should you choose?</p>
 <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
 <span>📅 อัปเดตล่าสุด: มิถุนายน 2026</span>
 <span>⏱️ 5 min read</span>
 </div>
 </header>

 <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-green-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-4">🎯 คำตอบด่วน</h2>
 <p class="text-lg text-green-800 leading-relaxed">
 <strong>eSIM is the easiest option</strong> if your phone supports it — buy online before you go, activate when you land, no physical card needed. If your phone doesn't support eSIM, buy a tourist SIM card at the airport arrivals hall. Expect to pay about <strong>100–300 RMB (~$15–$45)</strong> for a tourist SIM plan with data. Note that most tourist SIMs in China are data-only or have limited voice minutes.
 </p>
 </div>

 <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
 <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 ในคู่มือนี้</h3>
 <ul class="space-y-3">
 <li><a href="#esim" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📱 eSIM Providers (Airalo, Holafly)</a></li>
 <li><a href="#airport" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🏛️ Tourist SIM Cards at the Airport</a></li>
 <li><a href="#coverage" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📡 Coverage & Speed</a></li>
 <li><a href="#vpn" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🔒 What About a VPN?</a></li>
 </ul>
 </nav>

 <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
 <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

 <h2 id="esim" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
 <span class="text-4xl">📱</span> eSIM Providers
 </h2>

 <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
 <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">📡 Airalo</h3>
 <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
 <li><strong>Coverage:</strong> 4G/5G across China</li>
 <li><strong>Plans:</strong> 1 GB to 20 GB, 7 to 30 days</li>
 <li><strong>Activation:</strong> Buy and install before arrival, activates on landing</li>
 <li><strong>Price:</strong> ~$5–$30 depending on plan</li>
 <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Easy setup, no passport required, keep your home SIM</li>
 <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Data only (no Chinese phone number)</li>
 </ul>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
 <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">📡 Holafly</h3>
 <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
 <li><strong>Coverage:</strong> 4G/5G across China</li>
 <li><strong>Plans:</strong> Unlimited data for 5 to 30 days</li>
 <li><strong>Price:</strong> ~$20–$50 depending on plan</li>
 <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Unlimited data, simple pricing</li>
 <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Data only, more expensive than Airalo</li>
 </ul>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
 <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>Tip:</strong> Make sure to check the coverage areas of the packages. Some are only available in certain regions. If you're planning to visit more than one city, we suggest getting a package that covers the whole country.</p>
 </div>

 <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

 <h2 id="airport" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
 <span class="text-4xl">🏛️</span> Tourist SIM Cards at the Airport
 </h2>

 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">If your phone doesn't support eSIM or you want a Chinese phone number:</p>

 <div class="space-y-4 mb-12">
 <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl">
 <span class="text-blue-500 text-xl">📍</span>
 <div>
 <strong class="text-gray-900">Where to buy:</strong>
 <p class="text-gray-700">All major international airports have carrier counters in the arrivals hall — including Beijing Capital, Shanghai Pudong, Guangzhou Baiyun, Shenzhen Bao'an, and Hangzhou Xiaoshan. You'll also find SIM cards at convenience stores and vending machines, though these usually have limited plan options.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl">
 <span class="text-red-500 text-xl">🛂</span>
 <div>
 <strong class="text-gray-900">What you need:</strong>
 <p class="text-gray-700">Your passport (mandatory for SIM registration in China). Bring some cash or prepare Alipay/WeChat — not all counters reliably accept foreign cards.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl">
 <span class="text-green-500 text-xl">💰</span>
 <div>
 <strong class="text-gray-900">Expected cost:</strong>
 <p class="text-gray-700">Airport tourist SIM plans typically range from <strong>100–300 RMB (~$15–$45)</strong>, depending on data allowance, duration, and carrier. Prices vary by airport and promotions, so check the counters for current offers.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl">
 <span class="text-purple-500 text-xl">⏱️</span>
 <div>
 <strong class="text-gray-900">Setup time:</strong>
 <p class="text-gray-700">The whole process takes about 10–15 minutes at the carrier counter.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>

 <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

 <h2 id="coverage" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
 <span class="text-4xl">📡</span> Coverage & Speed
 </h2>

 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">All three carriers (China Mobile, Unicom, Telecom) offer excellent 4G coverage in cities and along high-speed rail routes. 5G is available in most urban areas. In remote/rural areas, China Mobile has the best coverage.</p>

 <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

 <h2 id="vpn" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
 <span class="text-4xl">🔒</span> What About a VPN?
 </h2>

 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">If you purchase a SIM card package, you may encounter issues with using Western software such as Google, WhatsApp, and Instagram. Therefore, you will need to use a VPN to access these applications — and you must complete the setup <strong>before</strong> arriving in China, as VPN websites may be inaccessible within China.</p>

 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">We've got a full guide covering which VPNs work in China, how to set them up, and tips to keep you connected:</p>

 <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
 <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>📖 Full guide:</strong> <a href="/th/life/vpn-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best VPNs for Traveling in China</a></p>
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 not-prose">
 <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 คู่มือที่เกี่ยวข้อง</h3>
 <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
 <a href="/th/life/vpn-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
 <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">🔒 Best VPNs for Traveling in China</p>
 <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Don't forget to set up your VPN before you go</p>
 </a>
 <a href="/th/life/survival-kit/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
 <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">🎒 Your China Trip Survival Kit</p>
 <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">The complete pre-travel checklist</p>
 </a>
 <a href="/th/payment/setup-alipay/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
 <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">💳 How to Set Up Alipay</p>
 <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Set up payment before you arrive</p>
 </a>
 <a href="/th/transport/didi/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
 <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">🚗 How to Use Didi in China</p>
 <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Getting around with ride-hailing</p>
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 <!-- แหล่งอ้างอิง -->
 <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
 <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">แหล่งอ้างอิง</h3>
 <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
 <li>SIM plans vary by carrier and region. Check China Mobile, China Unicom, or China Telecom at airport counters.</li>
 </ul>
 </div>
 </article>
</Layout>